 :verdict :refutes
 :headline
 "The receipt predicted 21 hops. The chain has 4 NODES, all of them segments, and
  ZERO legacy single-entry nodes. Its arithmetic rested on 18 pre-segmentation
  singles that it believed were still standing because 'only a fold consumes them';
  the mechanism is stated correctly but the fact is wrong -- a fold DID run, and
  this walk found the commit where it happened."

 :method
 {:what "Read the graph head pointer from R2, decoded the chain tip commit, then
         followed novelty-front and novelty-back to nil, classifying each node by
         the same test kotobase-peer.core/node-entries uses: a node containing an
         'es' key is a SEGMENT, otherwise it is a legacy SINGLE."
  :script "scripts/novelty-chain-shape.cljs (nbb)"
  :read-only "Every R2 call is `wrangler r2 object get`. No writes, no deletes, no
              deploys, no Worker or secret changes."
  :verification "Blocks are read through ipld.core/get-node, which recomputes the
                 CID from the bytes before decoding, so a store returning different
                 bytes under a CID fails closed rather than being counted."
  :authority ["protocols-worker/src/kotobase_protocols_worker/kotobase_r2.cljs -- block-key/head-key"
              "kotoba-lang/kotobase-peer src/kotobase_peer/core.cljc -- walk-novelty-entries, node-entries, push-novelty!"
