 :tooling-hazard-found
 {:what "ipld.core/link-cid returns nil under nbb, silently."
  :why "It is (.-cid l) on a `deftype Link`. nbb interprets the namespace with SCI,
        which stores deftype fields under a mangled property key (observed: `Kb`), so
        .-cid resolves to undefined. No throw, no warning."
  :blast-radius "Every link reads as 'no link'. The first run of this script walked
                 zero nodes and printed a confident `TOTAL nodes 0`. The same defect
                 reaches into the authority libraries: chain.core/commit-info computes
                 :prev the same way, so a history walk reports :prev nil and 'reaches
                 genesis' after one commit -- which it did here, announcing 'reached
                 genesis without seeing a fold' after scanning exactly 1 of 972
                 commits."
  :fix "Read the CID through the Link's own toString (`#ipld/link \"<cid>\"`), which
        is written in ipld.core's source rather than being an artifact of field
        layout, validate it against the base32 CIDv1 shape, and exit 2 if it cannot
        be parsed. Decode the commit envelope directly instead of using commit-info."
  :NOT-a-production-bug
  "This is a hazard of READING these namespaces with SCI. The deployed Worker is
   compiled by shadow-cljs, where a deftype field is a real property access, and it
   demonstrably hydrates. Nothing here is evidence about the running service."
  :how-it-was-caught "The scanned/expected denominator. 0 != 63 is loud; a bare
                      'TOTAL nodes 0' would not have been."}

 :discrimination
 {:why "A counting script that stops early and prints a small number is the exact
        defect this workspace polices, so the guard was shown to fire, not asserted."
  :cases
  [{:input "the live chain, unmodified"
    :result "SCANNED 63 / EXPECTED 63, exit 0"}
   {:broke "the `rest` traversal in walk! -- never follow the chain past the first node"
    :result "SCANNED 15 / EXPECTED 63, printed 'THE TWO COUNTS DISAGREE', exit 1.
             It did NOT report 1 node as the answer."}
   {:broke "the graph name, so the head pointer does not exist"
    :result "COULD-NOT-ANSWER, exit 2"}
   {:broke "one cached block's bytes, so it no longer hashes to its CID"
    :result "COULD-NOT-ANSWER (CID verification), exit 2"}]
  :exit-codes {0 "walk complete and the two counts agree"
               1 "walk complete but the counts disagree -- a real finding"
               2 "the walk could not be completed; neither pass nor fail"}
  :note "Exit 1 was also reached un-engineered during development, by the link-cid
         defect above (SCANNED 0 / EXPECTED 63)."}

